{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>From before</b> — The yod in חולי is superfluous, and it is the verb's name-letter, like לא יוכלו קום. And because the [letter] alef in מלך, ארץ was a word of trembling in pausal form (mil'eil), as if it were written חול תחול הארץ, or חולי as a command form, like קומי. And the meaning of הדין is that the earth should tremble. Now he will explain the reason for the dancing of the mountains."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 114, :notes {0 "The passage is textually difficult. 'באל\"ף ארץ' likely means the word ארץ appears with alef; the syntax connecting מלך, ארץ, and 'מלעיל' is compressed and possibly corrupt. 'מהדין' taken as 'the meaning of הדין' is uncertain; it may be a different reading or abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:41.738622225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}